# Invitation product

One Next.js app and one Vercel project. Templates are skins. A sale is content (names, date, photos) plus a template id — never a copied repo or a new Vercel app per client.

Keep event copy out of components; use the event content module (`src/content.ts` today). Shared blocks: hero, countdown, gallery, details, map, RSVP. Skins may hide or restyle blocks; do not fork the content schema without updating `docs/content-schema.md`.

One RSVP pipeline for all templates. Do not add a new email/sheet/db integration per skin.

Do not implement the full `docs/templates-catalog.md` list in one go. Next code step after docs: extract the current page into `templates/quiet-luxury`, then a second skin.

Read `docs/product.md` for deploy/URL model and `AGENTS.md` for the same rules.
